      {% call docs.subsection("principal-mapping", "Principal Mapping File") %}
{% call docs.markdownBlock() %}
Map Azure principal IDs to human-readable names for better role assignment reports. Create a JSON file with this structure:
{% endcall %}

{% call docs.codeBlock("principals.json") %}
{
  "users": {
    "12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012": "jane.doe@contoso.com",
    "87654321-4321-4321-4321-210987654321": "john.smith@contoso.com"
  },
  "groups": {
    "abcdef12-3456-7890-abcd-ef1234567890": "Platform Team",
    "fedcba98-7654-3210-fedc-ba9876543210": "Security Team"
  },
  "servicePrincipals": {
    "11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555": "terraform-spn",
    "66666666-7777-8888-9999-000000000000": "github-actions-spn"
  }
}
{% endcall %}

{{ docs.minorHeading("Generating Mapping Files with Azure CLI", "h4", "docs-minor-heading-xl") }}

{% call docs.markdownBlock() %}
Use Azure CLI to automatically generate principal mapping files from your Azure AD tenant:
{% endcall %}

{{ docs.minorHeading("Bash Script", "h5", "docs-minor-heading-script") }}
{% call docs.codeBlock("generate-principals.sh") %}
#!/bin/bash

echo '{'
echo '  "users": {'
az ad user list --query '[].{id:id,upn:userPrincipalName}' -o json | \
  jq -r '.[] | "    \"" + .id + "\": \"" + .upn + "\""' | \
  paste -sd ',' -
echo '  },'
echo '  "groups": {'
az ad group list --query '[].{id:id,name:displayName}' -o json | \
  jq -r '.[] | "    \"" + .id + "\": \"" + .name + "\""' | \
  paste -sd ',' -
echo '  },'
echo '  "servicePrincipals": {'
az ad sp list --all --query '[].{id:id,name:displayName}' -o json | \
  jq -r '.[] | "    \"" + .id + "\": \"" + .name + "\""' | \
  paste -sd ',' -
echo '  }'
echo '}'
{% endcall %}

{% call docs.markdownBlock() %}
Run `bash generate-principals.sh > principals.json`.
{% endcall %}

{{ docs.minorHeading("PowerShell Script", "h5", "docs-minor-heading-script-spacious") }}
{% call docs.codeBlock("Generate-Principals.ps1") %}
$mapping = @{
    users = @{}
    groups = @{}
    servicePrincipals = @{}
}

$users = az ad user list --query '[].{id:id,upn:userPrincipalName}' | ConvertFrom-Json
foreach ($user in $users) { $mapping.users[$user.id] = $user.upn }

$groups = az ad group list --query '[].{id:id,name:displayName}' | ConvertFrom-Json
foreach ($group in $groups) { $mapping.groups[$group.id] = $group.name }

$sps = az ad sp list --all --query '[].{id:id,name:displayName}' | ConvertFrom-Json
foreach ($sp in $sps) { $mapping.servicePrincipals[$sp.id] = $sp.name }

$mapping | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 3
{% endcall %}

{% call docs.markdownBlock() %}
Run `./Generate-Principals.ps1 > principals.json`.
{% endcall %}

{{ docs.minorHeading("Filtering for Specific Principals", "h5", "docs-minor-heading-script-spacious") }}

{% call docs.markdownBlock() %}
For large tenants, you may want to filter for specific principals instead of fetching all:
{% endcall %}

{% call docs.codeBlock("Bash - Filter by IDs") %}
PRINCIPAL_IDS=$(terraform show -json plan.tfplan | \
  jq -r '.resource_changes[]? | select(.type == "azurerm_role_assignment") | .change.after.principal_id' | sort -u)

echo '{"users":{},"groups":{},"servicePrincipals":{}}' > principals.json
for id in $PRINCIPAL_IDS; do
  az ad user show --id "$id" 2>/dev/null | \
    jq -r '{users: {($id): .userPrincipalName}}' || \
  az ad group show --group "$id" 2>/dev/null | \
    jq -r '{groups: {($id): .displayName}}' || \
  az ad sp show --id "$id" 2>/dev/null | \
    jq -r '{servicePrincipals: {($id): .displayName}}'
done | jq -s 'reduce .[] as $item ({}; . * $item)' > principals.json
{% endcall %}

{% call docs.markdownBlock() %}
Use the `--principal-mapping` option to replace GUIDs with names in role assignment reports.
{% endcall %}

{% call docs.codeBlock("Usage") %}
tfplan2md plan.json --principal-mapping principals.json
{% endcall %}

{{ docs.minorHeading("Using Principal Mapping with Docker", "h4", "docs-minor-heading-xl") }}

{% call docs.markdownBlock() %}
When running tfplan2md in a Docker container, mount `principals.json` into the container:
{% endcall %}

{% call docs.codeBlock("Docker - Mount from current directory") %}
docker run -v $(pwd):/data oocx/tfplan2md \
  --principal-mapping /data/principals.json \
  /data/plan.json --output /data/plan.md
{% endcall %}

{% call docs.codeBlock("Docker - Mount as read-only") %}
docker run \
  -v $(pwd)/plan.json:/data/plan.json:ro \
  -v $(pwd)/principals.json:/app/principals.json:ro \
  oocx/tfplan2md --principal-mapping /app/principals.json /data/plan.json
{% endcall %}

{% call docs.codeBlock("Docker - With debug output") %}
docker run -v $(pwd):/data oocx/tfplan2md --debug \
  --principal-mapping /data/principals.json \
  /data/plan.json --output /data/plan.md
{% endcall %}
      {% endcall %}
    {% endcall %}

    {% call docs.pageSection("code-analysis", "Static Code Analysis", "Integrate security findings from Checkov, TfLint, Trivy, and other SARIF-compatible tools directly into your Terraform plan reports.") %}
      {% call docs.subsection("code-analysis-overview", "Overview") %}
{% call docs.markdownBlock() %}
tfplan2md natively supports SARIF 2.1.0 format, enabling you to combine infrastructure changes with security findings in a single unified report.
{% endcall %}

{% call docs.codeBlock("Basic Usage") %}
# Generate Terraform plan
terraform show -json plan.tfplan > plan.json

# Run security tools
checkov -d terraform --framework terraform --output sarif -o checkov.sarif
tflint --format sarif > tflint.sarif
trivy config terraform --format sarif --output trivy.sarif

# Generate unified report
tfplan2md plan.json \
  --code-analysis-results "*.sarif" \
  --output report.md
{% endcall %}

{{ docs.minorHeading("What You Get", "h4", "docs-minor-heading-lg") }}

{% call docs.markdownBlock() %}
- **Summary Table:** High-level overview of findings by severity.
- **Resource Mapping:** Findings are automatically linked to affected resources and attributes.
- **Multi-Tool Support:** Combine results from multiple security tools in one report.
- **Severity Badges:** Visual indicators on resources show security status.
{% endcall %}
      {% endcall %}

